      "article": {
        "headline": "Bayern Munich loses Harry Kane for months following Cologne Bundesliga draw",
        "summary": "Bayern Munich and Cologne drew 1-1 in Friday's Bundesliga match, with Harry Kane suffering a syndesmosis ankle ligament injury.",
        "body": "Harry Kane was forced off in the 20th minute of Friday night's Bundesliga match after suffering a tear to the syndesmosis ligament in his left ankle. Club official Eberl and manager Vincent Kompany confirmed after the final whistle that the striker now faces a recovery period of several months. The injury occurred during a 1-1 draw against Cologne, adding to an extensive list of sidelined players for the German champions including Manuel Neuer, Alphonso Davies, and Serge Gnabry.\n\nThe loss of Kane, who was replaced by Tom Bischof early in the first half, presents a significant hurdle for Kompany. The manager had just returned to the dugout following a month-long absence due to illness. With key players like Michael Olise also exiting the match with a bruised foot and Jamal Musiala causing concern, Bayern's depth is being severely tested as they navigate a dense schedule. The draw leaves Bayern at 22 points, holding a one-point lead over Borussia Dortmund, who have the opportunity to move to the top of the table on Saturday.\n\nMikey Moore provided the opening goal for Cologne in the 12th minute following an assist by Said El Mala. Nathaniel Brown secured the equalizer for Bayern in the 37th minute after a setup from the substitute Bischof. Despite substitutions in the 70th minute bringing on Musiala and Kim Min-Jae, the score remained level until the final whistle.\n\nBayern now shifts focus to European competition. They are scheduled to travel to France to face Lille in the Champions League on Wednesday 25 November. Following that, they return to domestic league action with an away fixture in Hamburg on Saturday 28 November.",
